    "linked content id" : 14,
    "font" : "SFRM1095",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "As Ω is bounded, up to a subsequence, we may assume that yk converge to some point y¯ ∈ Ω. The continuity of u gives u(¯y) = 0, so that y¯ ∈ u−1(0). On the other hand,"
